{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-70935" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=5?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-70935" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =5 \\\\ (x-(-3))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & =(\\sqrt{5})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=-3,$ $b=-3,$ and $r=\\sqrt{5}.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-3,-3)$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{5}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-70935" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087dcd4dad46191d119e730e1a02a8fb43cfdbe00a99a48095018cfdfb3788bd"} {"question" "q-70935" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-70935" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "The center is $(-3,-3)$ and radius is $5$"] ["text" "The center is $(-3,-3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{5}$"] ["text" "The center is $(-3,3)$ and radius is $5$"] ["text" "The center is $(3,3)$ and radius is $5$"] ["text" "The center is $(3,3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{5}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-70935" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The center is $(-3,-3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{5}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-70987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/assets/b6a4e9a8f4a1c6dcaaad453b843896f3fc56ae22a37d481dcb4cfe54cc53361d.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(7,3)$ and $(-1,3)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-70987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is  \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(7,3)$ and $Y(-1,3),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{{(7-(-1))}^{2}+{(3-3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{8}{2}=4.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{7+(-1)}{2},\\frac{3+3}{2})=(3,3)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=4$ and center $(a,b)=(3,3),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-70987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087dcd4dad46191d119e730e1a02a8fb43cfdbe00a99a48095018cfdfb3788bd"} {"question" "q-70987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-70987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=16"] ["math" "(x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=4"] ["math" "(x+3)^{2}-(y+3)^{2}=4"] ["math" "(x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=16"] ["math" "(x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-70987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=16"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-72619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/assets/2ff035f38f5892f61d1eb037c7e39c59c8ec5104babac45224c4902152a0cfaa.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-1,-3)$ and the point $X(1,1)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-72619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(1-(-1))}^{2}+{(1-(-3))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & =(\\sqrt{20})^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-72619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087dcd4dad46191d119e730e1a02a8fb43cfdbe00a99a48095018cfdfb3788bd"} {"question" "q-72619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-72619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=20"] ["math" "(x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=2\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "(x+1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20"] ["math" "(x-1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20"] ["math" "(x-1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=2\\sqrt{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-72619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=20"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-117084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center and the radius of the circle with equation $(x+5)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=81?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-117084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =81 \\\\ (x-(-5))^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={9}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=-5,$ $b=3,$ and $r=9.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-5,3)$ and its radius is $9.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-117084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087dcd4dad46191d119e730e1a02a8fb43cfdbe00a99a48095018cfdfb3788bd"} {"question" "q-117084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-117084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "The center is $(-5,-3)$ and the radius is $9$"] ["text" "The center is $(-5,3)$ and the radius is $81$"] ["text" "The center is $(-5,3)$ and the radius is $9$"] ["text" "The center is $(5,-3)$ and the radius is $81$"] ["text" "The center is $(5,-3)$ and the radius is $9$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-117084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The center is $(-5,3)$ and the radius is $9$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-117103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/assets/08653e0cdc9bb404bd7ef193dfc9f1b5c0884002e83dd72cbcbda5779a2363a1.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(2,-1)$ and $(2,1)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-117103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(2,-1)$ and $Y(2,1),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(2-2)^{2}+(-1-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{2}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, we can find the center using the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{2+2}{2},\\frac{-1+1}{2})=(2,0)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=1$ and center $(a,b)=(2,0),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={1}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-117103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087dcd4dad46191d119e730e1a02a8fb43cfdbe00a99a48095018cfdfb3788bd"} {"question" "q-117103" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-117103" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1"] ["math" "(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4"] ["math" "(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1"] ["math" "(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"} {"question" "q-117103" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/state.json" "file_sha256" "612ca13e305e1ac92a453b147a7a2cda28d9bc580ed3a3366370059af3bdbde4"}] "usage" {} "basis" 734 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
